<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Operation 1027</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2023">2023</a>–<a href="/years/2024">2024</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myanmar-civil-war-2021-present">Myanmar civil war (2021–present)</a> · <a href="/encyclopedia/wars">All wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Operation 1027 was an offensive launched on 27 October 2023 by the Three Brotherhood Alliance of ethnic armed groups in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shan-state">Shan State</a>, Myanmar. It captured towns, military posts and border crossings with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, including Laukkai, and was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/military-junta">military junta</a>'s greatest defeat since the coup of 2021, encouraging resistance offensives elsewhere in the country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-1027.jpg" alt="Operation 1027" width="320" height="367" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Clyde H. Mapping · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Operation_1027.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Background</h2><p>The Three Brotherhood Alliance joined three ethnic armed organisations: the Myanmar National Democratic Alliance Army (MNDAA), of Kokang Chinese ethnicity, the Ta'ang National Liberation Army (TNLA) of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shan-state">Shan State</a> and the Arakan Army (AA) of Rakhine State. The military had long struggled to control the ethnic regions, recruiting mainly from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamar-people">Bamar</a> majority, and by late 2023 its resources were strained. Since the coup of February 2021 cyber-scam centres had spread along the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, run with Chinese criminal gangs and worked by trafficked people, and China pressed the junta to end them.</p><p>On 20 October 2023 fleeing prisoners at a scam facility in Laukkai, controlled by the former pro-military member of parliament Ming Xuechang, were killed by guards; reports put the dead at upwards of 80. The massacre has been credited with leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> to tacitly allow the offensive.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Course of events</h2><p>The alliance, able to draw on 15,000 troops, declared the operation on 27 October 2023, naming among its aims the end of military rule and of the online fraud along the border. The MNDAA attacked bases in Kokang at 4:00 am, seized Chinshwehaw and blocked the roads from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lashio">Lashio</a>, while the TNLA took camps in Namhkam Township. The regime answered with air strikes and shelling. By 28 November the alliance claimed to have taken over 220 junta positions, and offensives had spread to Rakhine State, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kayah-state">Kayah State</a>, Sagaing Region and Chin State.</p><p>A ceasefire in December soon collapsed. A second, brokered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> for northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shan-state">Shan State</a>, was agreed on 11 January 2024 but broke down in June, when the TNLA accused the junta of air strikes in breach of it and resumed its offensive; by 28 June it had captured Kyaukme, and with People's Defense Force units it had taken Nawnghkio.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Aftermath and significance</h2><p>Fighting closed the border posts at Muse and Laukkai and halted cross-border trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, and The Irrawaddy estimated the junta's lost tax revenue at US$423,000 a day. By 21 November 2023 an estimated 335,000 people had been displaced across Myanmar by the rebel offensives. The scam centres of the north were heavily damaged, and many Chinese nationals were sent back to China. Analysts weighed China's role against the rebels' own aims, many seeing the operation as part of Myanmar's Spring Revolution. By 2026, according to the BBC, the alliance's unity had weakened, and only the Arakan Army remained in active conflict with the military.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Operation 1027” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Since the coup of 2021 the military has faced People's Defence Forces and ethnic armies at once, and the Three Brotherhood Alliance's <b>Operation 1027</b>, launched in October 2023, took large areas of northern Shan State.</blockquote><a href="/empire/myanmar">Myanmar · Military</a></li></ul></section>
